[[File:Battledroid513_detail.png|thumb|right|250px|[[Battle droid 513]], a [[battle droid]] cobbled together by the [[Mandalorian]] [[Death Watch]] on [[Carlac]]]]
"'''Monster droid'''," or "'''junk droid'''," was a term used to describe any [[droid]] created by recombining spare parts of different origins. The [[Jawa]]s of [[Tatooine]] were known to build such amalgamated droids at the request of customers who needed specialized units.<ref name="AEYNTK">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]''</ref> [[JG-1]], formerly known as the Junk Giant, was a monster droid created by [[Taborr's gang]] during the [[High Republic Era]].<ref name="The Junk Giant">{{YJA|The Junk Giant}}</ref> [[Battle droid 513]] was a monster droid created by the [[Mandalorian]]s of [[Death Watch]] to use as target practice on the [[planet]] [[Carlac]].<ref name="A Friend in Need">{{TCW|A Friend in Need}}</ref> [[CR-8R]], who was built by [[Rhyssa Graf]] from a mash-up of different droid models, was technically a monster droid.<ref name="The Escape">''[[Adventures in Wild Space: The Escape]]''</ref> [[MA-13]] was a ferry droid and a monster droid.<ref name="Redemption">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 8: Redemption}}</ref>

